WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.501
-Guys, it is the end
of the week,

00:00:02.501 --> 00:00:04.004
and that's usually when I
catch up on some personal stuff.

00:00:04.004 --> 00:00:05.972
I check my inbox,
I return some e-mails,

00:00:05.972 --> 00:00:07.841
and of course I send out
thank-you notes.

00:00:07.841 --> 00:00:09.242
And I was just running
a bit behind,

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:10.610
so I thought, if you guys
wouldn't mind,

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:12.278
I'd like to write out
my weekly thank-you notes.

00:00:12.278 --> 00:00:13.780
right now, I hope
it's cool with you guys.

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:17.149
James, can I get some thank-you
note writing music, please?

00:00:17.149 --> 00:00:18.584
Can you, uh...

00:00:18.584 --> 00:00:20.653
♪♪
God, is he --

00:00:20.653 --> 00:00:23.489
♪♪

00:00:23.489 --> 00:00:25.291
Is he animatronic?
Is that a real...

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:26.425
[ Laughter ]

00:00:26.425 --> 00:00:28.027
Oh, there.
He moved his eyes.

00:00:28.027 --> 00:00:30.430
[ Laughter ]

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:31.931
♪♪

00:00:31.931 --> 00:00:33.833
Thank you,
Tampa Bay Lightning,

00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:35.935
for winning the Stanley Cup
on Monday night.

00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:37.570
And for somehow doing it
with less fighting

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:39.305
than we saw Tuesday night.

00:00:39.305 --> 00:00:41.608
[ Laughter ]

00:00:43.876 --> 00:00:45.111
♪♪

00:00:45.111 --> 00:00:47.213
Thank you, puffer coats,

00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:49.782
for making me look like
The Rock in a t-shirt.

00:00:49.782 --> 00:00:54.387
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.387 --> 00:00:55.721
He's just jacked.

00:00:55.721 --> 00:00:58.491
Puffer coats or puffy coats?
What are we?

00:00:58.491 --> 00:00:59.992
Puffer?

00:00:59.992 --> 00:01:02.561
I don't think I've ever
called them puffer coats.

00:01:02.561 --> 00:01:03.896
What do you call them?

00:01:03.896 --> 00:01:06.165
-Uh, puffer coats.

00:01:06.165 --> 00:01:07.833
-You just made it up.

00:01:07.833 --> 00:01:09.669
-No, I didn't.

00:01:09.669 --> 00:01:10.837
Yes, I did.

00:01:10.837 --> 00:01:12.204
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.204 --> 00:01:14.339
-I knew you did.
I knew you did.

00:01:14.339 --> 00:01:16.543
Okay.
♪♪

00:01:16.543 --> 00:01:19.045
-Thank you, surprise
"Borat" sequel coming out

00:01:19.045 --> 00:01:20.746
before Election Day.

00:01:20.746 --> 00:01:22.448
It's nice to know
that no matter who wins,

00:01:22.448 --> 00:01:25.485
we can all look forward to four
more years of co-workers saying,

00:01:25.485 --> 00:01:27.020
[ As Borat ] "My wife."

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:29.255
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:30.890
Let him do it.
Let him do it.

00:01:32.592 --> 00:01:33.893
♪♪

00:01:33.893 --> 00:01:35.895
Thank you, Microsoft Word,

00:01:35.895 --> 00:01:38.231
for suffering a major outage
this week,

00:01:38.231 --> 00:01:40.533
or as Clippy put it,
"Well, well, well,

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:42.535
look at who needs help now."

00:01:42.535 --> 00:01:45.138
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.939 --> 00:01:49.041
He gets a bad rap, Clippy.

00:01:49.041 --> 00:01:50.776
He always helped me out.
I like Clippy.

00:01:50.776 --> 00:01:52.144
-I love Clippy.
-Right?

00:01:52.144 --> 00:01:53.413
-He's my home boy.
-Yeah.

00:01:53.413 --> 00:01:57.650
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.650 --> 00:02:00.552
-But then you had the option
to turn Clippy off.

00:02:00.552 --> 00:02:03.022
-Yeah, but I liked him.
-You bring him back, right?

00:02:03.022 --> 00:02:04.490
-Yeah.
-Yeah, you bring him back.

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:06.458
-Bring him back.
-Come on, man.

00:02:06.458 --> 00:02:08.495
[ Laughs ]
Clippy.

00:02:08.495 --> 00:02:10.296
-Yeah.

00:02:10.296 --> 00:02:11.831
♪♪

00:02:11.831 --> 00:02:14.600
-Thank you, knowing there's
a mosquito in my bedroom,

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:16.336
for providing me
with a fun night

00:02:16.336 --> 00:02:17.937
of randomly slapping myself.

00:02:17.937 --> 00:02:21.273
[ Laughter ]

00:02:21.273 --> 00:02:26.312
-[ Imitating buzzing ]

00:02:31.117 --> 00:02:33.419
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:36.823
♪♪

00:02:36.823 --> 00:02:39.058
-Thank you, scented markers,

00:02:39.058 --> 00:02:40.893
for telling you all
who the druggies

00:02:40.893 --> 00:02:42.562
in the first grade class
would be.

00:02:42.562 --> 00:02:45.598
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.598 --> 00:02:48.434
-Yeah. Yeah.
-"Jared, Jared, stop."

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:50.903
-Yeah.

00:02:50.903 --> 00:02:53.239
-I like this one.
♪♪

00:02:53.239 --> 00:02:55.708
This one you have to
really look at the graphic.

00:02:55.708 --> 00:02:57.609
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:02:57.609 --> 00:02:59.178
It'll be worth it.
It'll be --

00:02:59.178 --> 00:03:01.881
This is almost like it's --
this is like AR.

00:03:01.881 --> 00:03:04.984
XR. Multi screen type of stuff.
-Oh, okay, okay, okay.

00:03:04.984 --> 00:03:06.885
-Yeah. This is like -- yeah.

00:03:06.885 --> 00:03:08.087
Anyways...

00:03:08.087 --> 00:03:10.056
Look at the graphic and also
listen to me.

00:03:10.056 --> 00:03:12.057
-Okay.
-So it is like an --

00:03:12.057 --> 00:03:13.593
it's an audio,
it's an audible, it's --

00:03:13.593 --> 00:03:14.727
-I get it.
-Yeah.

00:03:14.727 --> 00:03:16.195
-All right.

00:03:16.195 --> 00:03:17.930
-Wait, at the same time, or --?
-At the same time?

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:19.899
Was that -- Yeah, yeah.
-Okay.

00:03:19.899 --> 00:03:21.967
-At the same time, you're
going to look and listen.

00:03:21.967 --> 00:03:23.269
Yep.

00:03:23.269 --> 00:03:24.737
-Right now?

00:03:24.737 --> 00:03:27.606
-Soon, yeah. Soon as I --
Soon as I can.

00:03:27.606 --> 00:03:29.175
-Okay.
-All right. Thanks, Higgins.

00:03:29.175 --> 00:03:30.243
-You ready? Let's do it.

00:03:30.243 --> 00:03:34.747
[ Laughter ]

00:03:34.747 --> 00:03:38.351
-Take that back, man.
-Oh, my God.

00:03:38.351 --> 00:03:39.919
Take it like this.

00:03:39.919 --> 00:03:41.120
♪♪

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:43.256
Thank you, hammerhead sharks,

00:03:43.256 --> 00:03:45.491
for being a fearsome predator
that's also really good

00:03:45.491 --> 00:03:47.226
at giving side-eye.

00:03:47.226 --> 00:03:51.164
[ Laughter ]

00:03:51.164 --> 00:03:54.700
[ Applause ]

00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:56.202
That's really good.

00:03:57.903 --> 00:03:59.338
♪♪

00:03:59.338 --> 00:04:02.341
-Thank you, London Marathon,
for being held this Sunday

00:04:02.341 --> 00:04:05.444
without spectators,
or as I'll put it on Monday,

00:04:05.444 --> 00:04:07.647
"Hey, everybody, I ran
the London Marathon."

00:04:07.647 --> 00:04:09.215
[ Laughter ]

00:04:09.215 --> 00:04:11.050
There you have it.
Those are my thank-you notes.

